    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## The PCA \"Hidden Logic\"\n",
        "* **PC1 (The Volume Driver):** Dominated by **Total SqFt** and **Full Baths**. This is the market’s \"Size Filter\"—it separates the sprawling estates from the starter homes.\n",
        "* **PC2 (The Quality Signal):** Captures the relationship between **Main SqFt** and **Fireplaces**. This explains why \"Main Floor Living\" commands a premium even when total square footage is identical.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Strategic Market Segmentation\n",
        "* **The \"Main Floor\" Premium (Cluster 0 vs. 4):** Despite sharing nearly identical **Total SqFt (~3,200)**, Cluster 0 commands a **$120k premium** over Cluster 4. The PCA confirms this is driven by superior Main Floor area and bedroom count.\n",
        "* **The Luxury Slab-on-Grade (Cluster 5):** The highest-priced segment (**$680k avg**). Uniquely, their `Main SqFt` almost perfectly matches `Total SqFt`, identifying a high-spec \"Ranch\" or single-level luxury archetype that buyers prioritize.\n",
        "* **The Efficiency Split (Clusters 2 & 3):** These sub-800 SqFt properties are mathematically separated by a **$41k gap**, purely based on fireplace presence and minor utility differences—the \"Tiny Home\" market's internal hierarchy.\n",
        "\n",
        "# PUMA Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "## PUMA Scree"
      ],
      "id": "c7d82818"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
