    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## PUMA Feature Importance"
      ],
      "id": "84242b11"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: puma_feature_importance\n",
        "plot_pca_loadings(puma_pca_model, puma_features, \"PUMA\")"
      ],
      "id": "puma_feature_importance",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## PUMA PCA Factor Analysis"
      ],
      "id": "0180f31d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: puma_pca_heatmap\n",
        "plot_pca_heatmap(puma_pca_model, puma_features)"
      ],
      "id": "puma_pca_heatmap",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## The PCA \"Hidden Logic\"\n",
        "* **PC1 (The Capacity Driver):** Unlike the residential set, PUMA's first component is heavily influenced by **Garage Capacity** and **GLA (Gross Living Area)**. This represents the \"Utility Anchor\"—how many cars and how much total space the property provides.\n",
        "* **PC2 (The Subterranean Signal):** A massive differentiator in this data is **Basement SqFt**. PCA identifies this as a primary axis of variance, effectively splitting the market between properties with massive lower-level footprints and those built on slabs or crawlspaces.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Strategic Market Segmentation\n",
        "* **The \"Basement Premium\" (Cluster 3):** This is the highest-priced segment (**$554k avg**). PCA highlights this group not just for its size, but for its massive **Basement SqFt (1,444)** and high **Bedroom count (4.8)**. It represents the \"Large Family\" archetype.\n",
        "* **The Garage/Lot Combo (Cluster 0):** Commands a high price (**$470k**) despite having **zero basement space**. PCA shows this value is driven by the **Garage Capacity (2.44)** and **Lot Acres (0.18)**—prioritizing external utility over internal basement square footage.\n",
        "* **The High-Density Efficiency (Cluster 4):** The clear outlier with the lowest price (**$190k**). PCA groups these based on minimal GLA (657) and near-zero garage/basement capacity.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Market Comparison: Residential vs. PUMA\n",
        "\n",
        "## Dimensionality of Value\n",
        "* **Residential Strategy:** Value is driven by **\"Main Floor Dominance.\"** The PCA shows that buyers pay a premium for how the primary living space is finished (Fireplaces/Main SqFt), even when total square footage is equal.\n",
        "* **PUMA Strategy:** Value is driven by **\"Total Capacity.\"** The math reveals a market segmented by **Basement SqFt** and **Garage Capacity**. In this dataset, \"Expansion Potential\" is the primary axis of variance.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Side by Side Comparison\n",
        "| Metric | Residential Driver | PUMA Driver |\n",
        "| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n",
        "| **Primary PCA Axis** | Total SqFt / Full Baths | GLA / Garage Capacity |\n",
        "| **Secondary PCA Axis** | Main SqFt / Fireplaces | Basement SqFt / Lot Acres |\n",
        "| **Value Outlier** | Executive Layouts (Cluster 3) | Large Family Basements (Cluster 3) |\n",
        "| **Market Split** | Lifestyle & Layout | Utility & Expansion |\n",
        "\n",
        "## Final Synthesis\n",
        "> By using **PCA-based clustering**, we’ve demonstrated that different sectors of the property market have fundamentally different mathematical structures. \n",
        ">\n",
        "> * **Residential** is a market of **Design**: where the square footage is located matters most. \n",
        "> * **PUMA** is a market of **Utility**: where the total capacity for storage and family growth dictates the price.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Random Forest"
      ],
      "id": "9b79fb22"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: random_forest\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create Log Targets\n",
        "res_target_log = np.log1p(res_df['Sold Price'])\n",
        "puma_target_log = np.log1p(puma_df['Sold Price'])\n",
        "\n",
        "def run_log_rf(df_features, target_log, cluster_labels, title):\n",
        "    from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestRegressor\n",
        "    from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
        "    from sklearn.metrics import mean_absolute_error, r2_score\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Feature Prep\n",
        "    X = df_features.copy()\n",
        "    X['Cluster'] = cluster_labels\n",
        "    X = pd.get_dummies(X, columns=['Cluster'], prefix='C').fillna(0)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Split\n",
        "    X_train, X_test, y_train_log, y_test_log = train_test_split(X, target_log, test_size=0.2, random_state=42)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Train\n",
        "    rf = RandomForestRegressor(n_estimators=100, n_jobs=-1, random_state=42)\n",
        "    rf.fit(X_train, y_train_log)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Predict\n",
        "    y_pred_log = rf.predict(X_test)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Convert back to Dollars for Evaluation\n",
        "    y_test_dollars = np.expm1(y_test_log)\n",
        "    y_pred_dollars = np.expm1(y_pred_log)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Calculate Real-World Error\n",
        "    mae_dollars = mean_absolute_error(y_test_dollars, y_pred_dollars)\n",
        "    r2 = r2_score(y_test_log, y_pred_log) # R2 is calculated on the log scale\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Plot\n",
        "    plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
        "    plt.scatter(y_test_log, y_pred_log, alpha=0.5, color='darkblue')\n",
        "    plt.plot([y_test_log.min(), y_test_log.max()], [y_test_log.min(), y_test_log.max()], 'r--')\n",
        "    plt.title(f\"{title} (Log-Scale) Performance\\nR² = {r2:.2f} | Avg Error = ${mae_dollars:,.0f}\")\n",
        "    plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "    return rf, X_train, X_test, y_train_log, y_test_log\n",
        "\n",
        "def get_model_report_card(res_model, res_X_test, res_y_test, puma_model, puma_X_test, puma_y_test):\n",
        "    from sklearn.metrics import mean_absolute_error, r2_score\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Residential: Predict in Log, convert to Dollars\n",
        "    res_pred_log = res_model.predict(res_X_test)\n",
        "    res_r2 = r2_score(res_y_test, res_pred_log)\n",
        "    res_mae_dollars = mean_absolute_error(np.expm1(res_y_test), np.expm1(res_pred_log))\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # PUMA: Predict in Log, convert to Dollars\n",
        "    puma_pred_log = puma_model.predict(puma_X_test)\n",
        "    puma_r2 = r2_score(puma_y_test, puma_pred_log)\n",
        "    puma_mae_dollars = mean_absolute_error(np.expm1(puma_y_test), np.expm1(puma_pred_log))\n",
        "    \n",
        "    report = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "        \"Metric\": [\"R-Squared (Accuracy)\", \"Mean Absolute Error ($)\"],\n",
        "        \"Residential Model\": [f\"{res_r2:.3f}\", f\"${res_mae_dollars:,.2f}\"],\n",
        "        \"PUMA Model\": [f\"{puma_r2:.3f}\", f\"${puma_mae_dollars:,.2f}\"]\n",
        "    })\n",
        "    \n",
        "    return report\n",
        "\n",
        "def get_feature_importance_table(model, X_train, title):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Returns a table of the top 5 most influential features for the model.\"\"\"\n",
        "    importances = model.feature_importances_\n",
        "    feature_names = X_train.columns\n",
        "    \n",
        "    feat_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "        'Feature': feature_names,\n",
        "        'Importance (%)': importances * 100\n",
        "    }).sort_values(by='Importance (%)', ascending=False).head(5)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    feat_df['Dataset'] = title\n",
        "    return feat_df"
      ],
      "id": "random_forest",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Residential Random Forest"
      ],
      "id": "fc6541a6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: res_rf\n",
        "res_rf, res_X_train, res_X_test, res_y_train, res_y_test = run_log_rf(\n",
        "    res_features, \n",
        "    res_target_log, \n",
        "    res_l_clusters, \n",
        "    \"Residential\"\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "res_rf",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## PUMA Random Forest"
      ],
      "id": "c9af8d33"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: puma_rf\n",
        "puma_rf, puma_X_train, puma_X_test, puma_y_train, puma_y_test = run_log_rf(\n",
        "    puma_features, \n",
        "    puma_target_log, \n",
        "    puma_l_clusters, \n",
        "    \"PUMA\"\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "puma_rf",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Performance"
      ],
      "id": "8f352584"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: model_report_card\n",
        "get_model_report_card(res_rf, res_X_test, res_y_test, puma_rf, puma_X_test, puma_y_test)"
      ],
      "id": "model_report_card",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
